ch.proxy_endpoint`, and this stack sets none. It also states\nthat native `web_search` is parked so nobody spends a turn rediscovering the 400.\n**Tool output stays out of the parent context** makes that\ntool use delegated work: the child returns a digest - numbered findings, each one\nclaim, one source URL and at most two lines of support, no raw result dumps,\nconfidence stated - and keeps the raw pages to itself."],[1414,"What the check catches"],[1424,"What the check catches, and what it deliberately leaves alone"],[1119,"What the container mounts, and what \"be the host\" costs"],[1808,"What the fix changed, and how to land it:"],[2059,"What the model rules out: long-lived `development`/`staging`/`production` branches; \"merge to\ndevelopment first\"; a release branch that has to be kept forever; cherry-picking a fix from one\nenvironment branch to another; and a flag platform nobody asked for."],[1478,"What the scaffold repository ships, and the account-wide gaps it closes"],[1470,"What the scaffold ships"],[65,"What the startup script does, in order"],[39,"What the two templates make"],[85,"What the two templates make, and when the `devcontainer` toggle matters"],[1417,"What this deliberately does not do"],[560,"What this is not"],[957,"What this is not"],[911,"What to read next"],[1267,"What was measured"],[1994,"What you see is `gh: command not found`, or `fix` refusing with `cannot install the\ncredential helper - gh is not installed in this environment; install gh (apt install gh,\nor the pinned copy the golden image ships) and run this again`. `check` reports the same\nhole honestly: with no gh there is no `gh stored login` slot to read, and a chain with\nnothing else in it prints `NO GitHub credential`."],[1963,"What you see is one of: `remote: Invalid username or token. Password authentication is\nnot supported for Git operations.`, `remote: Repository not found.`, `fatal:\nAuthentication failed for 'https://github.com/...'`, or `fatal: could not read